<http://data.silknow.org/object/36be1fcb-26a2-33a7-b549-0a508550c733>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Silk parasol and cotton slip cover, England, 1865-1870"@en , "Parasol of green silk, unlined. Pagoda shape with a pointed bone tip and wooden crook handle. Ribs and stays are of japanned metal with a circular section. There are brass wire catches to hold it open and shut. The rib tips are of japanned metal surmounted by small bone knobs. Machine-stitched. With a slip cover of natural brown cotton holland and hand-stitched."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/ea881264-1f54-3386-b4c4-b18c3ff74a25> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Silk parasol and cotton slip cover, England, 1865-1870"@en , "Parasol of green silk, unlined. Pagoda shape with a pointed bone tip and wooden crook handle. Ribs and stays are of japanned metal with a circular section. There are brass wire catches to hold it open and shut. The rib tips are of japanned metal surmounted by small bone knobs. Machine-stitched. With a slip cover of natural brown cotton holland and hand-stitched."@en ;
